      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لَهُ قَوْلُ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ: «۝ وَ لِلّٰهِ عَلَى اَلنّٰاسِ حِجُّ اَلْبَيْتِ مَنِ اِسْتَطٰاعَ إِلَيْهِ سَبِيلاً ۝» قَالَ «يَخْرُجُ يَمْشِي إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ عِنْدَهُ شَيْءٌ» قُلْتُ لاَ يَقْدِرُ عَلَى اَلْمَشْيِ قَالَ «يَمْشِي وَ يَرْكَبُ» قُلْتُ لاَ يَقْدِرُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ قَالَ «يَخْدُمُ اَلْقَوْمَ وَ يَخْرُجُ مَعَهُمْ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2504 - Ali ibn Abi Hamzah narrated from Abu Basir, from Abu Abdullah (as), who said:\nI asked him about the verse of Allah (swt), the Exalted: \"And [due] to Allah (swt) from the people is a pilgrimage to the House—whoever is able to find thereto a way\" (Surah Aal-E-Imran 3:97).\nImam (as) replied: \"He should set out on foot if he has nothing.\"\nI said: \"What if he cannot walk?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Then he should walk and ride.\"\nI said: \"What if he cannot do that either?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Then he should serve the group and set out with them.\""
        ]
      }
    },
